############################################################
# FINDINGS (L=50ms sweep) — reverted to 700 after; committed demo UNCHANGED
############################################################
# VALIDITY NOTE: the inline env-check printed 700 — an artifact of `kubectl rollout
#   restart` immediately followed by `rollout status` (status returned the OLD generation
#   as "complete" before the restart cycled). The storm nonetheless ran at L=50: median
#   request = 72ms is impossible at L=700 (every cache-miss floors at 700ms via pg_sleep),
#   and CPU/pod was 4-8x the L=700 runs. Both independently confirm L=50 was active.
#
#                       L=700 (committed demo)     L=50 (this experiment)
#   autoscaling         2 -> 7 -> 2                 2 -> 5 -> 2   (concurrency-driven; latency-independent)
#   CPU / pod (load)    ~20-70m  (idle, 10-35%)     ~200-286m  (100-143% of the 200m request)
#   regime              I/O-bound (CPU-HPA blind)   CPU-bound  (a CPU-HPA WOULD now fire)
#   median latency      ~700ms+                     72ms
#   p90 / p95           >> 200ms                    124ms / 170ms   (both UNDER the SLO)
#   p99 / max           seconds                     > 200ms (k6 threshold FAILED) / 5.11s
#   throughput          ~70-77 rps                  ~528 rps avg (113,537 reqs total)
#
# INTERPRETATION (validates the REPORT #4 "latency knob / CPU<->I/O spectrum" note):
#  1. Lowering L makes the SLO reachable for the BULK (median/p90/p95 all < 200ms) and
#     shifts the bottleneck to CPU (idle -> saturated). At L=50 a plain CPU-HPA would also
#     fire -- empirical proof of the regime flip.
#  2. The autoscaler still scales correctly (2->5->2): concurrency is latency-independent.
#  3. p99 STILL crosses 200ms -- but now from the SPIKE-ONSET TRANSIENT (max 5.11s: requests
#     queued during the ~40s before pods scaled up), NOT the store floor (which is 50ms).
#     => Reactive scaling's onset lag, not SLO reachability, is the binding constraint.
#        This is a STRONGER argument for predictive pre-scaling than the 700ms floor was.
